<Content title="Privacy policy" description="Your attendance calculations stay in your browser. Here is what that means, and what happens when you visit or contact us." path="/privacy-policy" eyebrow="Your information">
 <p class="updated">Updated 27 September 2026</p>
 <h2>Attendance inputs</h2><p>BunkMeter calculates attendance on your device. This release does not send your entered counts, target, session class actions or future previews to a server. These values are held in page memory and clear when you refresh or close the page.</p>
 <h2>Accounts, storage and tracking</h2><p>The site does not require an account. This release does not use cookies, local storage or a cloud database to save attendance. It includes no third-party analytics, advertising or payment scripts. Fonts and calculator assets are served with the site.</p>
 <h2>Visiting the website</h2><p>Your browser must contact our hosting infrastructure to load the site. Hosting providers may process ordinary request information such as IP address, browser information, requested URL and request time to deliver and secure the website. This is distinct from the attendance figures you type. We do not promise that visiting a website involves no data processing.</p>
 <h2>If you email us</h2><p>Sending an email shares your email address and message with BunkMeter and the email services involved. We use that information to handle your request. Avoid sending sensitive information. You can ask about access, correction or deletion of correspondence through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>; applicable requirements and provider retention may affect what can be deleted.</p>
 <h2>Students and personal information</h2><p>You do not need to provide a name, age, institution, student ID or medical information to use the calculator. Please do not send these details unnecessarily, including in bug reports.</p>
 <h2>Other websites and changes</h2><p>Links to other services are governed by those services’ practices. If we later introduce saved records, analytics or advertising, we will explain the change here and implement any required choices before enabling it.</p>
 <p>For privacy questions, <a href="/contact">contact BunkMeter</a>.</p>
</Content>
